{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patch-set 2 CI follow-up RCA: the canary test monkeypatches the shared time.sleep module. Under Ubuntu CI load, repo-isolation subprocess.run reached Popen._wait timeout backoff before fixture teardown, and subprocess internally called that patched sleep, causing the unrelated canary fixture to fail. A deterministic held-out regression closes the child capture pipes while leaving it alive, proving the exact Popen._wait -> time.sleep path. The repair captures the original sleep primitive and temporarily gives only subprocess internals a stable sleep namespace around each bounded Git probe, restoring shared state in finally while leaving the test monkeypatch untouched. RED on patch set 2; GREEN after repair; deleting the stable binding returns the oracle to RED. The affected isolation, canary, and subprocess-environment matrix passes 70 tests; make lint and make typecheck pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787084582781560001,"uuid":"fcda0a8c-dab4-4c75-99b3-b3ff7c2eec28"}